As for Telecommunication, whether it’s a data center, server room, or the building’s communication lines, there is a designated space (often referred to as a “space”) for swapping or installing equipment. This space is typically led by the electrical discipline but is actually managed by the low-voltage (weak current) discipline, serving as the equivalent of the electrical room for the high-voltage (strong current) discipline.

Generally, tasks like wiring jumpers for high-voltage or low-voltage systems, as well as final testing of IT computers—including Network setup, topology, or software—are handled by the IT team, not us. These are the standards used for Telecommunication Design, with the U.S. national standard being TIA/EIA Big C.
